# How to cite FerrumDeck.
#
# No DOI: there is no deposit backing one. A DOI here would be a fabricated
# identifier, and this repository has a claims-integrity gate specifically to
# stop that class of claim. If a Zenodo (or equivalent) deposit is ever made,
# add `doi:` and `identifiers:` then — not before.
#
# If you are citing a *measurement* rather than the software, cite the artifact
# that carries it, not this file. The coherence-monitor false-positive rate is
# published per provenance in `docs/reports/coherence-fp-2026-09.md`, and every
# run is recorded, append-only, in `docs/eval-health-series.jsonl` with its
# measurement date, producing commit and harness version. Read the report's
# "What this corpus is not" section before quoting the headline figure.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FerrumDeck in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software

title: "FerrumDeck"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, in-path enforcement engine and AgentOps control plane for
  agentic AI workflows. Every tool call an agent attempts passes through a
  policy decision before it executes: deny-by-default tool allowlists,
  five-layer Airlock runtime inspection, budget gates with leases, an R1-R3
  reversibility ladder, AP2 and x402 payment spend gates, approval gates, and a
  hash-chained audit trail with out-of-band checkpoint anchoring. Regulatory
  rules ship as first-class policy modules (EU AI Act Article 50 transparency,
  Colorado SB 26-189). Governance behaviour is measured by deterministic,
  offline evaluations committed to the repository rather than asserted in prose.

authors:
  - family-names: "Jain"
    given-names: "Sattyam"
    email: "sattyamjain96@gmail.com"
    alias: "sattyamjjain"

repository-code: "https://github.com/sattyamjjain/ferrumdeck"
url: "https://sattyamjjain.github.io/ferrumdeck/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.8.18"
date-released: "2026-09-05"

keywords:
  - "ai-agents"
  - "agent-security"
  - "policy-enforcement"
  - "agentops"
  - "llm-security"
  - "audit-trail"
  - "eu-ai-act"
  - "rust"
